    "fileId": 60671,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "c-Met pathway",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "A transmembrane receptor tyrosine kinase known as c-Met is encoded by &lt;em&gt;MET&lt;/em&gt;, located on chromosome7, having as its ligand HGF. Functionally, c-Met signalling involves GAB1, PI3K, STAT3, and RAS inducing cell proliferation, cell motility, cell survival, and remodelling of the extracellular matrix, contributing to cancer survival, invasion, and metastasis. The HGF/c-Met pathway is disrupted in patients with hereditary papillary renal carcinoma as the result of germline, activating variants in the tyrosine kinase domain of c-Met as well as non-random duplication of the chromosome arm on which the mutated &lt;em&gt;MET&lt;/em&gt; allele is located. PSI, plexin, semaphorin, integrin cysteine-rich domain; IPT, immunoglobulin-like regions in plexins and transcription factors.",
    "source": "Katia R.M. Leite",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/5/60671.jpg",
